{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>If perhaps your way was turned.</b> Like 'were it not' (לוּלֵי). Sometimes אוּלַי serves in the sense of לוּלֵי." "<b>And you too I would have slain.</b> This is an inverted verse (מְסֹרָס), and it is as if it says: 'And I would have slain you too' — that is to say, not the pressing alone did I call against you through me, but the slaying as well." "<b>And her I kept alive.</b> And now, because she spoke and rebuked you, and you could not withstand her rebuke — as it is written <b>And he said, No</b> — I killed her, so that they should not say: this is the one that silenced Balaam with her rebuke and he could not answer. For the Omnipresent is mindful of the dignity of creatures. And similarly (Leviticus 20): ״וְהָרַגְתָּ אֶת הָאִשָּׁה וְאֶת הַבְּהֵמָה״, and similarly (ibid.): ״אֶת הַבְּהֵמָה תַּהֲרֹגוּ״ (Tanḥuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:19.140783913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}